WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short time,

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.880
daily episode 505.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.600
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.260
Today is June 9th, 2026.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.060
There's a lot to cover in Tesla land today.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.120
Multiple cybercabs at an Atlanta service center

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.480
show Tesla is moving physical hardware

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.700
into real world preparation ahead of any unsupervised launch.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.100
Multiple cybercabs were photographed

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.920
at a service center near Atlanta.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.840
The sightings add Georgia to the growing list

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.940
of locations where the vehicles have appeared.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.960
This follows earlier observations in California and Texas

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.200
and points to broader pre-launch testing activity.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.040
The images were shared by a Reddit user

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.320
and reposted by Tesla Rottie.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.420
Tesla cybercabs have now been documented

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.080
in 16 states plus Washington, DC.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.660
The list includes California, Texas, Illinois, New York,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.440
Massachusetts, Michigan, Florida, Arizona,

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.600
Colorado, Oklahoma, Virginia, Georgia, Nevada,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.120
Missouri, Pennsylvania, and Washington.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.620
The pattern shows testing activity across both coastal

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:07.620
and central regions.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.760
This geographic spread indicates Tesla

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.020
is distributing test vehicles more widely

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.520
than previously documented.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.660
Observers are tracking whether the pattern points

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.980
to specific regulatory test corridors

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.620
or simply broader durability runs.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.020
While Tesla moves test hardware

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:28.140
into real service locations, another automaker

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.000
is preparing a direct product challenge in showrooms.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.640
A first drive of the Rivian R2 positions it

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.560
as the first vehicle to directly challenge the Model Y

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.860
in size, price, and capability.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.140
Reviewers noted the R2 matches or exceeds the Model Y

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.760
in several practical areas.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.920
Rivian aims to move from niche luxury sales

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.580
to broader market competition

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.720
with this smaller, lower priced SUV.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.060
Early drives of the 2027 Rivian R2 suggest

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.440
it could prompt some owners to consider switching.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.200
The vehicle targets a lower price point

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.580
while offering comparable range and utility.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.360
Rivian sees the R2 as the model

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.260
that could make it a mainstream brand.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.420
Reviewers say the Rivian R2 delivers

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.760
where legacy automakers have fallen short.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.180
The vehicle matches the Model Y in key areas

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.560
while adding distinctive design and features.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.640
This positions Rivian as the first credible volume rival

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.500
in the segment.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.300
The R2 addresses most owner complaints

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.340
while leaving a few gaps in the initial drive experience.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.280
Reviewers noted strong performance and packaging

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.080
but flagged specific areas still needing refinement.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.680
Rivian is using these early drives

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.220
to refine the production version.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.720
As external competition sharpens,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.420
someone Wall Street are already looking past vehicles

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.060
altogether.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.780
Analysts are shifting focus from Tesla's vehicle sales

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.960
to its robotics and AI ambitions.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.180
The commentary argues that long-term value

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.660
will come from optimists and related programs

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.340
rather than automotive margins.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.740
This view is gaining traction

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.200
ahead of any major robot taxi deployment.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.380
The shift in focus comes as vehicle margins face pressure

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.780
and robot taxi timelines remain uncertain.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.760
This view treats optimists and related AI work

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.280
as the primary growth driver going forward.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.400
That robotics emphasis ties directly

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.200
into the practical questions raised

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.360
in today's first principle segment.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.880
Tesla posted that it supervised full self-driving software

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.540
does not waste driver time during operation.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.960
The message reinforces the current supervised systems value

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.120
while unsupervised capability remains under regulatory review.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.560
It comes as the company continues

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.240
incremental version updates.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.840
A Tesla driver was recorded apparently a sleep at the wheel

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.420
on a California highway.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.180
The incident highlights ongoing questions

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.780
about driver attention during supervised FSD use.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.720
It follows repeated regulatory scrutiny

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.340
of driver monitoring systems in partially automated vehicles.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.060
The contrast highlights ongoing regulatory scrutiny

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.160
of driver monitoring.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.880
Before we close, a couple of short segments put these threads

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.260
into wider context.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.880
The global mail opinion piece argues Tesla is deprioritizing

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.400
traditional vehicle manufacturing in favor

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.320
of autonomy and robotic spits.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.580
This shift risks leaving core product quality

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.760
and customer experience under-resourced

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.660
if robot taxi timelines slip.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.460
Tesla's continued software updates

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.600
and service network expansions remain the main counter

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:36.380
to that concern.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.560
Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.600
the steady appearance of cybercabs in service centers

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.220
across more states challenges the assumption

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.680
that regulatory approval is the only remaining bottleneck

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.980
before wider deployment.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.520
The pattern of sightings now spans 16 states plus DC,

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.280
showing Tesla has moved beyond a handful

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.520
of controlled test routes.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.580
This distribution implies the company is already stress testing

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.760
logistics such as charging, maintenance,

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.200
and transport between locations rather than waiting

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.580
for final legal clearance.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.200
If the goal is a scalable robot taxi network,

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.780
these early physical movements reveal

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.840
where the real constraints lie, parts availability,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.920
technician training, and regional permitting

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.360
for even limited operations come into focus.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:28.660
Watching how quickly Tesla can expand the service center footprint

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.800
will indicate whether the vehicle itself

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.280
or the supporting infrastructure becomes

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.340
the tighter limit on rollout speed.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.880
Kathy Wood asked how Tesla plans to manage

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.900
parking and traffic violations once robotaxies

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.240
operate without drivers.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.280
The question followed her experience riding

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.200
in a supervised vehicle and highlights

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.440
a practical operational detail still being worked out.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.300
It adds to the list of regulatory and logistical items

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.060
that must be resolved before wider deployment.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.020
Some cyber truck owners received surprise

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.060
free supercharger access that was later modified.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.940
The brief change and subsequent adjustment

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.340
created confusion among early owners

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.580
about what benefits would actually remain.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.540
It illustrates how Tesla continues to tweak

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.720
ownership perks even after delivery.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.340
Fix auto-slaw in the UK received official

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.600
Tesla approved body shop status.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.240
The certification allows the facility

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.480
to handle Tesla repairs under manufacturer guidelines.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.820
It expands the network of authorized service points

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.740
outside Tesla's own centers.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.900
Keep an eye on how the expanding service network

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.200
supports wider cyber cab testing in the coming weeks.

